\title{RAVEL: Recovering Assortment-Adjusted Variance Explained by Genetic Liabilities}
\description{
Structural equation modeling framework for estimating direct and indirect genetic effects on offspring phenotypes using parent-offspring trio data with polygenic scores. RAVEL accounts for measurement error in PGS, assortative mating, hidden genetic variants not captured by the PGS, cross-parent tagging confounds, and population stratification. The method uses latent variable modeling with multiple PGS indicators to correct for measurement error and provides unbiased estimates of direct child effects, maternal effects, paternal effects, and the degree of assortative mating.

A structural equation modeling framework for estimating direct and indirect
